---
title: "publishSaleResults (LegionSealedBidAuctionSale)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_caller: Legion operator publishes results
    q_check_caller --> q_check_locked: caller is Legion operator
    q_check_caller --> q_revert_auth: unauthorized
    q_check_locked --> q_check_not_published: cancelLocked == true
    q_check_locked --> q_revert_not_locked: cancellation not locked
    q_check_not_published --> q_set_results: results not yet published
    q_check_not_published --> q_revert_published: already published
    q_set_results --> q_set_key: claimMerkleRoot, acceptedCapitalMerkleRoot, totalTokensAllocated, totalCapitalRaised set
    q_set_key --> q_verify_key: privateKey = _privateKey
    q_verify_key --> q_emit: verify privateKey corresponds to stored publicKey
    q_verify_key --> q_revert_key: key pair mismatch
    q_emit --> [*]: emit SaleResultsPublished(claimMerkleRoot, totalTokensAllocated, privateKey)
    q_revert_auth --> [*]: revert Unauthorized
    q_revert_not_locked --> [*]: revert CancellationNotLocked
    q_revert_published --> [*]: revert AlreadyPublished
    q_revert_key --> [*]: revert InvalidPrivateKey

    note right of q_verify_key
        INV-001: Published private key must derive the same public key stored at initialization
        INV-002: After publication, anyone can decrypt sealed bids for verification
        INV-003: Results publication is irreversible
    end note
